course: dictionary
lesson: 11260
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. The best way to find the right one is to look at the words around it. «Wrap» is a good example. It can be an action, a thing or part of a phrase, and the sentence shows which one.
explain: «Ice or frozen peas should be wrapped in a cloth and used for about 15 to 20 minutes at a time, because ice on bare skin can burn.» Here wrapped means covered by folding cloth around something. The word cloth and the warning about burning skin show that it is not about a present.
explain: «Palaeontologists dig slowly, map where each bone lies, and wrap big bones in plaster jackets, like a cast on a broken arm, to carry them safely.» Wrap means covering something to keep it safe. The clue is the words to carry them safely. Always test your meaning in the sentence: does covering them still make sense? Yes, so you have it right.
explain: Some wrap words are not about covering at all. «Wrap up warm» means dress warmly, and «wrap up» can also mean finish. Ask: what word would fit here? If your meaning makes the sentence sensible, you have found the right one.
fact: To wrap means to cover something by folding paper, cloth or plastic around it.
fact: To wrap also means to put your arms or a scarf around someone.
fact: A wrap is a thin flat bread rolled around a filling.
fact: Wrap up can mean to finish, or to dress warmly.
fact: Bubble wrap is a material for wrapping things, but plastic bags and wrap are not toys because they can block breathing.
exercise: «Wax crayons are made of melted coloured wax poured into moulds, cooled, checked and wrapped in paper labels by machine.» What does wrapped mean here? | *Covered by folding paper around them | Pulled apart into pieces | Lit up with bright light | Sold quickly at a shop
exercise: Mum says, «Wrap up warm, it is freezing outside.» What does wrap up mean here? | Start a fight | Get lost in the snow | *Dress warmly | Give a present
exercise: «Red pandas wrap their thick tail around themselves like a blanket.» What does wrap mean here? | *To put something around and cover closely | To fold a flat bread | To shout loudly | To finish quickly
test: Lunch is a wrap with chicken and salad. What is a wrap here? | A bandage on a sprain | *A thin flat bread rolled around a filling | A blanket for winter | A present with a bow
test: «Adam hugged his sister and wrapped his arms around her.» What does wrapped mean here? | *Put his arms around her | Lifted her onto a shelf | Covered her in paper | Tied her hands together
exam: Which phrase means to finish? | bubble wrap | *wrap up | cling wrap | wrap around
